 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates tool input against the declared JSON Schema `inputSchema` before calling the executor. Required fields, declared property types and `enum` values are enforced; unknown extra properties pass through unchanged, and no coercion or defaults are applied. A schema rejection is returned as a `ToolResponse` (not thrown), so the orchestrator feeds it back to the model for correction within the existing `maxToolRounds` budget. Static schemas are compiled once at `register` time (a broken schema fails startup, not mid-conversation); function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` schemas are compiled per call and cached by object reference.
+
+**Migration note:** An executor that previously hand-validated its input now receives only input the schema already accepts. A tool that relied on seeing malformed input to produce its own error message will no longer see that input — the registry returns the rejection `ToolResponse` before invoking the executor. This is a MINOR version bump.
+
